WEBVTT

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.250
"Koto Club"
"#21    Meaning and Role"

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.250
"Koto Club"
"#21    Meaning and Role"
I wondered what it was about when
you told me to come in at 5:00 am.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.950
You've been starting your practice
this early every day?

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.790
No wonder you're always here first.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.290
Aren't you sleepy, though?
You're not exactly a morning person.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.870
I wanna dive into my bed right now.

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:06.330
The ensemble by Hozuki and
Miss Dojima was incredible.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:07.660
Yeah.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.700
All this time,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.750
I've been thinking that I should be able
to play like Hozuki by nationals,

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:14.500
but I might've been wrong.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.870
What do you mean?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:26.080
I feel we should find our own way
and stand alongside her.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:29.200
"Find our own way"?

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.080
Takinami said something about

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.370
thinking about the meaning
and role of our sound, right?

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.290
Well, I still don't know the answer at all,

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:43.200
but I think it goes beyond just playing
each note with care and skill.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.790
True. I thought... I had to
practice harder, too, but...

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:53.370
Chika... Seriously... I sometimes feel
like you're leaving me in the dust.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:57.950
But... "we"... huh?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:02:59.370
Okay!

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.540
Let's give a 17-string performance
grand enough

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.500
to match Hozuki's performance!

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.620
Yeah!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.000
--First, we'll double our current practice time.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.910
--Hey, Chika... I wanna make sure that I
stand alongside you, too, you know.
--First, we'll double our current practice time.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.790
--Hey, Chika... I wanna make sure that I
stand alongside you, too, you know.
--Do you know how many hours are in a day?

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.410
You and Mizuhara are becoming
in tune for the second koto part.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.120
Yeah! Kota has been practicing super hard!

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:23.450
You and Mittsu seem to be doing well
without any problems.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.290
Mittsu's performance sounds
delicate and beautiful.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:27.660
Yeah!

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.370
But... our first koto performance is plain.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.200
What?!

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.580
It's kinda serious.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.410
It's not a laughing matter! We're told

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.080
that the expression of
the piece changes depending on

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:44.700
how the first and second kotos
are played together, you know!

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:48.410
This has been bothering me for quite
some time... "Serious and boring."

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.700
What? It's not boring! It's cool!

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:52.950
What?

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.700
Being "serious" is cool!

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:03.200
So make the best of it. You guys on
first koto play with some serious style.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:06.620
And we, the second koto,
aim to make it lively.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.080
And...

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.040
Hey, Kurata! Are you listening?!

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.620
Yes, I'm listening! I'm sorry!

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:21.040
Oh? Miss Dojima! You're early.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.410
Adachi...

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.080
Are you okay today?

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.040
What?

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.700
Your eyes. If you get dust in them again

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:29.580
or something happens,
please don't hesitate to tell us.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.120
I'll probably be okay.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.660
That's good.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.080
Whoa! I'm the first here! Lucky me!
I can have Miss Dojima all to myself!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.910
Please give me special training
until the others come!

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:53.370
You've been working very hard, Adachi.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:58.290
You think so? But Chika works
a lot harder than I do.

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:00.540
He can play better and has
a better ear for music than me,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.830
but he practices a lot more than I do.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:07.370
Mr. Takinami was talking about
the meaning and the role of our sound.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:11.330
I think Chika has a reason to feel this
is really important to him for sure...

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:15.580
But to be honest, my sound doesn't...

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.410
A-Anyway, I'll work hard so that
I won't hold the others back.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:23.660
Your sound harmonizes very well
with all the others'.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:24.500
What?

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:30.870
Mr. Takinami told me the reason why
he picked you for the 17-string.

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:34.080
The sound quality of our club
members are all different, right?

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.580
So if things go wrong, the music could
become completely disorganized.

00:05:38.580 --> 00:05:42.450
But Adachi's sound harmonizes very well
with all those different sounds.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:46.290
It connects everyone's sound very nicely.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:52.830
That's why he assigned you the 17-string,
which is the core of the piece.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.200
He said so, and I agree with him.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:00.080
It connects... everyone's sound...

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.790
Thank you very much...

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.250
I'll work hard!

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.450
"Koto Club"

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.450
"Koto Club"
Sane.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.040
Did you change how you play?

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:17.660
What? You think so? I can't tell
a difference myself, though.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:22.250
It might be because I figured out
the meaning and role of my sound.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.790
What? You did?! What is it?!

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:27.290
What? It's a secret.

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:29.080
It's embarrassing to say it myself.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:29.950
--Don't "it's a secret" me!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:33.040
--Satowa. Did you change how you play a little?
--Don't "it's a secret" me!

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.620
Yes. My index finger has always been weak.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:40.950
I do think it's getting a lot better lately,

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:43.000
but after I heard your performance,

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.660
I realized I still had
a long way to go after all.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.950
I'm having a hard time giving
every note the same weight.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.660
If you'd like, please use this.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:56.540
Play wearing this. I often practice that way.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:00.330
Your total attention goes to your ears
and your senses get finely honed,

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.250
which makes it easier to
converse with your own sound.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:08.660
You can have it, so try it
when you practice alone.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:11.120
Thank you very much.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.290
You're welcome.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.790
I have to hurry up and move forward, too.

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:29.870
"Chika Kudo"

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.040
"Chika Kudo"
I have to hurry up and stand alongside her.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:34.790
I have to hurry up and stand alongside her.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:37.660
I have to... hurry up...

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:44.540
Crap... I feel kinda woozy.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:49.500
Oh, good morning. I was finally able
to come in before you.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.000
Four-eyes...

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.120
You've been practicing
this early every day, huh?

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:55.200
Not really...

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.700
I'm a total morning person,
so I wake up early.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:04.040
Well, it's not convincing
when you look so sleepy.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:07.250
Kudo. Aren't you overdoing it
with practice lately?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:10.330
Hm? What do you mean? I'm not overdoing it.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.950
Rather, I'm not practicing enough.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:15.750
We've got only one month
before the competition.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:21.370
His fingers...! Just how much
has he been practicing...?!

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:22.660
You're practicing too much!

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.540
I said it's not enough!

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:28.620
As it stands, we can't go to nationals!
I have to practice more!

00:08:28.620 --> 00:08:32.870
I do get how you feel, but you're
still a first-year student!

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.120
So don't be so hasty.

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.790
You'll still have a chance next year to--

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.080
Next year won't work for you guys!

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.750
Next year... will be too late.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.410
If you get it, move. You're in the way of--

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:53.750
I forbid you to practice!

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.080
--What?!
--Doing it too much is counterproductive!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:59.120
Shut up! I can't get better
without practicing, you idiot!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:01.000
I'm telling you to think about how you do it!

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.950
Shut the hell up!

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.120
--Hey! I said no practice!
--Let go of me!

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:12.000
Dammit! What are we doing?
We wasted a lot of time.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.580
It was a good diversion, wasn't it?

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:20.330
There's something I've been wondering...

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.160
...about your sound.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:23.660
Wh-What is it?!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.410
Your sound... sometimes shines...

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:29.080
"Sh-Shines"...?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.160
Yeah. Sometimes.

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.500
It shines...

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.450
...very gently...

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.660
...and warmly.

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:42.410
I've been curious what that sound
is about all this time...

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.910
But I think I finally know what it is.

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:51.250
That sound is your soul itself.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.450
It's your soul itself.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:01.830
Shoot! I said exactly what
I thought without thinking!

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:06.410
What the heck? You must've
hit your head or something.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.160
I shouldn't have said that.

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:11.040
Hey, Chika.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:16.580
You know sound? It touches people's souls.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:22.200
And pieces of music are the souls
of the people who create them.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:26.160
I don't know what this piece
means to you, but...

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:28.580
To tell you the truth,
I played this piece hoping

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:31.660
that people would smile after listening to it.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:35.120
See the entire piece thoroughly.
Understand its flow.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:42.080
Akira. We have guests,
so please prepare some tea for them.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:43.410
Guests?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.700
Mr. Takagi... The others are all senior
members of the Hozuki School, too.

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:54.000
Come see them later to say hello.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:58.120
Make tea for the grand master, too.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:10:59.250
Grandmother.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:03.540
Is it okay... for me to sit in the meeting, too?

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:09.250
Sure. Come with me.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:13.500
Hmph. I don't like the look in her eyes...

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:16.410
But she won't be able to do anything anyway.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:19.870
Well, she can just sit there and watch quietly.

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.580
Since Akira is taking her time
shutting down that club,

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:28.290
I'll put an end to it for good.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:31.290
What is this about?

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.500
"I wanna do it, too."

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:41.330
I called for this meeting in order to
discuss the grand master's daughter.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:45.950
She was excommunicated after causing
trouble for the school before

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:50.540
and now, she is about to
jeopardize the school again.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.120
"Jeopardize the school"?

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:58.540
Satowa belongs to a koto club
at her high school right now.

00:11:58.540 --> 00:12:04.040
But it's only a koto club in name.
They're a group of delinquents.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.200
Oh, I'm sorry. It was just anticlimactic, so...

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:12.580
That's Mr. Takagi's son...

00:12:12.580 --> 00:12:14.330
I wondered what this was about.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.660
The excommunicated daughter's club activities?

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:20.450
It's not something we, adults,
have to meet and--

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:25.700
Even if one of the delinquents has
gotten into trouble with the police?

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:28.290
"Strawberry Au Lait"

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:29.580
"Strawberry Au Lait"
Oh? Chika. Aren't you going to
the lunch-break practice today?

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.750
Oh? Chika. Aren't you going to
the lunch-break practice today?

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:35.580
That damn four-eyes forbade me
to go until my hand heals.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.620
Your hand?

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:41.200
Oh, I get it. You practiced like an idiot,
right? Use your head at little.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.500
Shut up.

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.540
Satowa. You're going to the practice now?

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:45.410
Yeah.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:49.000
Well then, see you later.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:49.830
Kudo...

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:51.450
Got a minute?

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:52.290
Huh?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.700
Ahhh! What's going on?!

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.250
--Is he gonna confess his love?!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:58.160
--I was worried about Satowa,
so I investigated the club.
--Is he gonna confess his love?!

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:02.700
I heard that one of the club members
named Kudo is a famous delinquent.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:07.870
He got in trouble with the police
many times due to his violence.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.160
Violence?!

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:13.330
It seems that his grandfather is a koto maker.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:17.580
This is hard to believe, but he even caused
an outrageous incident last year,

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:22.370
attacking his grandfather's house
with his delinquent friends.

00:13:22.370 --> 00:13:24.080
Attack?!

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:27.750
Rather than just a delinquent,
that sounds like he's a criminal.

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:31.500
Kudo did...?

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:34.700
I really wanna know what
kind of piece "Tenkyu" is.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.410
"What kind"?

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.540
I wanna know what kind of situation
you were in at the time,

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:45.790
what you were thinking,
and who you created this piece for.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.830
My granddad said...

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:56.160
...that pieces of music are "the souls
of the people who create them."

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:02.160
So I don't wanna play it without
knowing those things.

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.290
Actually, since I've been playing it
without knowing them,

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.410
I feel like something has been
missing all this time.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:10.870
It'll be a story solely about my family.

00:14:10.870 --> 00:14:14.040
Is that gonna help your performance?

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:16.000
It'll help a lot!

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.540
Okay.

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:25.410
You're saying that Satowa is hanging out
with such a dangerous boy?

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:30.330
Yes. Satowa must hate Hozuki
since she was excommunicated.

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:33.870
This boy and Satowa being in
a koto club together made me think...

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:39.750
...that they might be plotting
something like "revenge."

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.080
Play one more time.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:46.200
We're not neglecting them.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:49.660
I threw a tantrum on that big stage.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.580
I-I'd like to play... with you.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:59.540
Satowa's actions at the competition
severely demeaned the Hozuki name.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:04.500
We must do everything to prevent
further damage to Hozuki's reputation.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:09.000
We'll ask the school to disband the club
and have Satowa transfer to another--

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:10.620
How stupid...

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.450
What?

00:15:13.450 --> 00:15:19.000
You couldn't hear me? I said, "How stupid."

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.040
Akira...? What're you--?

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:26.250
I've held my tongue as you talked,
but "revenge"? That's ridiculous.

00:15:26.250 --> 00:15:31.200
How can you say things like that when
you don't know anything about Kudo?

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:34.620
You're the one who's plotting
something, right, Grandmother?!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.120
You've been secretly snooping
around on high school students

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.080
and now you're just saying whatever,
whether it's true or not!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.370
You're the one who is outrageous,
Grandmother!

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:47.120
Do you know this student Kudo?

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:51.790
Yes. I've been giving lessons
to that koto club.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.080
The idea they're plotting
"revenge" is nonsense.

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.870
I see. Then--

00:15:55.870 --> 00:16:00.660
Akira! You poor dear!
It must be that you're exhausted!

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:04.950
You must not know what you're saying.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.700
No, I do know very well what I'm saying.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:11.500
But <i>you </i>should take a second
look at yourself, Grandmother.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:12.330
Wha...?!

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.910
It's true... that due to
the preconceptions I had,

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:20.580
I just assumed that the students
were not serious about the koto.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.290
But I was wrong.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.330
Kudo and Satowa, and of course,
the other members too,

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:29.790
face the koto very seriously.

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:32.500
They just purely love the koto...

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:34.700
...and want to become better at it.

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:39.500
You're the only one who cannot
always face the koto, Grandmother!

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:43.870
All you think about
are things like your position,

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:47.080
making the school famous,
and dragging others down.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:50.660
Why don't you stop that and face
the koto for a change?

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:55.660
A-A-Akira... Who do you think
you're talking--?

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.450
Ms. Dojima...

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:02.120
That's enough. You put your granddaughter
in this difficult position.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.000
Mr. Takagi...

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.370
Akira. Is this student Kudo really someone

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:12.120
who's going to be harmful
to Satowa or the Hozuki School?

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:16.080
I don't know what he was like in the past,

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:23.330
but right now, his attitude towards
the koto is very earnest and sincere.

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:27.620
I see.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:31.910
What do you guys think? I don't think
we need to be concerned right--

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:35.040
Hold on a second, please!
Even if he's not causing problems now,

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:37.790
human nature doesn't change so easi--

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.830
That's enough!

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:42.750
No further discussion
on this subject is necessary.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:46.410
Ms. Dojima. Please show them out.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:47.290
You, too, Grand Master?!

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.750
Also...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.750
I won't allow you to investigate
my daughter and her friends

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:55.580
and say whatever you like!
I find it repugnant!

00:17:55.580 --> 00:17:58.660
Although I did excommunicate her...

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:01.160
...she's still my daughter.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:07.370
Grand Master.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:10.200
She feels that club and her friends
are precious enough for her

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:14.910
to even get down on her hands and
knees to ask a favor of me, right?

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:16.790
I think so.

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:19.370
Then that's fine.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:22.120
The qualifier for nationals
will be held next month.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.040
Satowa will perform, too.

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:27.700
Grand Master, why don't you come see it?

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:30.500
I no longer have...

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.450
...the right to do that.

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:41.580
Mr. Takagi. I'm sorry for behaving
like that in front of everyone.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:42.620
That's okay.

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.250
I was relieved to find out

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:48.290
that Hozuki still has a young person
like you with such backbone.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:51.410
I look forward to your successful future.

00:18:51.410 --> 00:18:53.910
Thank you very much.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:56.160
Hmph! Backbone, he said?!

00:18:56.160 --> 00:19:00.750
That club is full of troublemakers.
I bet they'll cause trouble someday.

00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:03.620
When they do, don't come crying to me!

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.950
So it was like that...

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.790
...up to the point when "Tenkyu" was created.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:20.250
I see.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:22.540
Got it. Thanks.

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.790
Hey, do you mind telling the others
what you just told me?

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:29.620
What?

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:33.750
I finally feel like I can figure out
how I should play that piece.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:36.330
But stories about my family would only be...

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:40.080
It might irritate us if it were a family story
of someone we don't care about,

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:42.370
but it's different in your case.

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:43.660
Different?

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:49.620
We do care about you.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:55.500
Well, I'm not gonna force you, though.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:59.370
Why... is Kudo always like this?

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:02.200
Always...

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:08.120
Kudo. I'll treat you to a Paplico.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.790
What?! Why?!

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.200
I just felt like it.

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:13.450
I wonder someday...

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:16.200
...if I could return...

00:20:16.200 --> 00:20:20.700
...the same amount of warmth...
you gave me...

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:25.080
Someday...

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:26.250
"Koto Club"

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:27.620
"Koto Club"
There.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:28.580
"Koto Club"

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:33.410
The spot where it livens up while
each part becomes the theme in turn...

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:36.500
Can you make those handoffs smoother?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.830
Smoother?

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:40.910
So smooth that the listener
can't tell when they happened.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:44.660
And, from there, it's like you'll
gradually show your own tone color.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:46.500
You can sing to your heart's content.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:48.910
Just make sure you lock down the tempo.

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:50.410
I see...

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.450
This is the best part of the piece,
so play with your sound

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:55.500
to your heart's content.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:56.830
And Hozuki.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:21:02.000
You play the start of the piece very softly,
but can you make it a little tense?

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:03.910
Tense?

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:09.000
You're probably doing it unconsciously,
but your sound is overall gentle.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:13.000
You seem to completely deny your
performance from the competition,

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.910
but that sound had an incredible power.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:18.450
Don't get rid of it. Make the best use of it.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:23.000
By putting that sound in the piece,
the other parts will shine more.

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.790
Okay.

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:36.620
Sounds like it'll be an amazing performance.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:40.000
I wonder when the last time was...

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.040
...that I felt excited like this...

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:43.540
"Keishi"

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.080
Thus...

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:49.910
...with each of us conveying
our feelings in our sound...

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.120
"Ms. Chiharu Hozuki"

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.450
...the qualifier for nationals...

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:08.750
...was about to begin.

00:23:50.040 --> 00:23:52.290
Next time, "Morning of the Showdown."

00:23:52.290 --> 00:23:54.370
"#22    Morning of the Showdown"
